From ea063876281328d6a5996c6cce7e6a528b6c20c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Singh <nathan.singh@hotmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 08:44:17 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Arena: a cup's trophy appears in the lobby straight after the
 first clear

The trophy rows' flag conditions were read only when the scene loaded, so the
trophy showed after a reload. ArenaSeries_Cleared now reads the scene's
placement table again (Event_SpawnActorPlacements) after setting the flag: the
rows whose condition now holds get their actors. The attendant's menu, the
manager's stock and the Djinn read the progress byte live and were right already.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 games/tbs/src/scene/arena_series.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/games/tbs/src/scene/arena_series.c b/games/tbs/src/scene/arena_series.c
index c12036e079..a1e25f0524 100644
--- a/games/tbs/src/scene/arena_series.c
+++ b/games/tbs/src/scene/arena_series.c
@@ -146,8 +146,12 @@ static void ArenaSeries_Cleared(s32 cup, const struct ArenaCupInfo *info) {
     FieldGameFlag_SetByte(FLAG_ARENA_SIDE_CLEARED,
                           FieldGameFlag_GetByte(FLAG_ARENA_SIDE_CLEARED) |
                               (1 << (cup - ARENA_MAIN_CUPS)));
-  // The trophy of the cup stands in the lobby from the next time it is built.
+  // The trophy of the cup stands in the lobby at once: the scene's placement
+  // rows are read again, which creates the actors whose condition now holds (and
+  // sets the others back in their places; they stand still).
   GameFlag_Set(FLAG_ARENA_TROPHY_FIRST + cup);
+  if (gFieldWork->tables[1] != NULL)
+    Event_SpawnActorPlacements(gFieldWork->tables[1], ACTOR_FIRST_PLACED);
   Event_SetMessageId(info->firstMsg);
   FieldMessage_ShowAtActor(ACTOR_ATTENDANT, 0);
   if (info->raiseTo != 0)
